<title>JAPAN: Keisei Electric falls on loss-cut sales.</title>
<headline>Keisei Electric falls on loss-cut sales.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Keisei Electric Railway Co Ltd shares fell on loss-cutting sales in the Monday morning session, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0113 GMT, the shares were 31 yen lower at 930 yen. It was the most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo exchange in a trade of 1.59 million shares.  </p>
<p>&quot;The market has run out of incentives to trade the shares on since details concerning the listing of Oriental Land Co Ltd were decided,&quot; a &quot;big four&quot; brokerage broker said.</p>
</text>
